NO RULER IS RESOLVED. An elasticity is a ratio of logs: no ridge, no bandwidth, no
compute peak, no fitted level. The reference clock is resolved on the pod for the
LEVEL RECORD only, and LEVEL excludes nothing here on either side; DRIFT and
host-bound are the two exclusions and V4 holds them to 20% of all rows.

